sword in the Password field.\n  3. Press the `Enter` key on the keyboard.\n* **Expected Result:** \n  - User is successfully authenticated.\n  - User is redirected to the Dashboard page.\n* **Test Type:** Functional / Positive\n* **Priority:** Medium\n* **Coverage Classification:** Positive Scenario / Usability\n\n---\n\n### **TC-LOG-003: Login Failure with Unregistered Email**\n* **Test Case ID:** TC-LOG-003\n* **Requirement Reference:** AC-04\n* **Title:** Verify error message when attempting to log in with an unregistered email address.\n* **Preconditions:** \n  - User is on the Login page.\n* **Test Data:** \n  - Email: `unregistered.user@example.com`\n  - Password: `ValidPassword123`\n* **Test Steps:**\n  1. Enter an unregistered email in the Email field.\n  2. Enter any valid password format in the Password field.\n  3. Click the "Login" button.\n* **Expected Result:** \n  - Login fails.\n  - An appropriate error message is displayed (e.g., "Invalid email or password" or "Email not found").\n  - User remains on the Login page.\n* **Test Type:** Functional / Negative\n* **Priority:** High\n* **Coverage Classification:** Negative Scenario / Error Handling\n\n---\n\n### **TC-LOG-004: Login Failure with Incorrect Password**\n* **Test Case ID:** TC-LOG-004\n* **Requirement Reference:** AC-05\n* **Title:** Verify error message when attempting to log in with a correct email but incorrect password.\n* **Preconditions:** \n  - User must be registered in the system.\n  - User is on the Login page.\n* **Test Data:** \n  - Email: `registered.user@example.com`\n  - Password: `WrongPassword999`\n* **Test Steps:**\n  1. Enter a valid registered email in the Email field.\n  2. Enter an incorrect password in the Password field.\n  3. Click the "Login" button.\n* **Expected Result:** \n  - Login fails.\n  - An appropriate error message is displayed (e.g., "Invalid email or password").\n  - User remains on the Login page.\n* **Test Type:** Functional / Negative\n* **Priority:** High\n* **Coverage Classification:** Negative Scenario / Error Handling\n\n---\n\n### **TC-LOG-005: Validation Error for Empty Email or Password**\n* **Test Case ID:** TC-LOG-005\n* **Requirement Reference:** AC-06, Business Rules\n* **Title:** Verify validation messages are displayed when email or password fields are left blank.\n* **Preconditions:** \n  - User is on the Login page.\n* **Test Data:** \n  - Case A: Email = `""`, Password = `""`\n  - Case B: Email = `"registered.user@example.com"`, Password = `""`\n  - Case C: Email = `""`, Password = `"ValidPassword123"`\n* **Test Steps:**\n  1. Leave fields empty based on Test Data combinations (A, B, or C).\n  2. Click the "Login" button.\n* **Expected Result:** \n  - Login action is blocked.\n  - Inline validation messages appear for the empty mandatory field(s) (e.g., "Email is required", "Password is required").\n* **Test Type:** Input Validation\n* **Priority:** High\n* **Coverage Classification:** Input Validation / Boundary Condition\n\n---\n\n### **TC-LOG-006: Password Field Masking**\n* **Test Case ID:** TC-LOG-006\n* **Requirement Reference:** AC-07\n* **Title:** Verify that characters entered in the password field are masked (hidden).\n* **Preconditions:** \n  - User is on the Login page.\n* **Test Data:** \n  - Password: `SecurePassword123!`\n* **Test Steps:**\n  1. Focus on the Password input field.\n  2. Type characters into the Password field.\n* **Expected Result:** \n  - Entered characters are visually masked (displayed as dots, bullets, or asterisks like `••••••••••••`).\n* **Test Type:** Security / Functional\n* **Priority:** Medium\n* **Coverage Classification:** Security / Edge Case\n\n---\n\n### **TC-LOG-007: Validation of Invalid Email Formats**\n* **Test Case ID:** TC-LOG-007\n* **Requirement Reference:** AC-11, Business Rules\n* **Title:** Verify system rejects various invalid email address formats.\n* **Preconditions:** \n  - User is on the Login page.\n* **Test Data:** \n  - `plainaddress`\n  - `@missingdomain.com`\n  - `username@.com`\n  - `username@domain..com`\n* **Test Steps:**\n  1. Enter an invalid email format into the Email field.\n  2. Enter a valid password.\n  3. Click the "Login" button.\n* **Expected Result:** \n  - Form submission is prevented.\n  - Email format validation error message is displayed (e.g., "Please enter a valid email address").\n* **Test Type:** Input Validation\n* **Priority:** High\n* **Coverage Classification:** Input Validation / Negative Scenario\n\n---\n\n### **TC-LOG-008: Password Minimum Length Boundary Condition**\n* **Test Case ID:** TC-LOG-008\n* **Requirement Reference:** Business Rules (Password >= 8 characters)\n* **Title:** Verify password boundary behavior for length constraints.\n* **Preconditions:** \n  - User is on the Login page.\n* **Test Data:** \n  - Pass1: `1234567` (7 characters - Invalid boundary)\n  - Pass2: `12345678` (8 characters - Valid boundary)\n* **Test Steps:**\n  1. Test Pass1: Enter valid email and 7-character password -> Click Login.\n  2. Test Pass2: Enter valid email and 8-character password -> Click Login.\n* **Expected Result:** \n  - Pass1 triggers a validation error stating minimum 8 characters are required.\n  - Pass2 passes length validation (attempts backend authentication).\n* **Test Type:** Boundary Value Analysis\n* **Priority:** Medium\n* **Coverage Classification:** Boundary Conditions\n\n---\n\n### **TC-LOG-009: Account Lockout after 5 Consecutive Failed Attempts**\n* **Test Case ID:** TC-LOG-009\n* **Requirement Reference:** AC-10, Business Rules (Max failed attempts: 5)\n* **Title:** Verify account is locked after 5 consecutive failed login attempts.\n* **Preconditions:** \n  - A registered user account exists.\n  - User is on the Login page.\n* **Test Data:** \n  - Email: `locked.user@example.com`\n  - Wrong Password: `IncorrectPassword`\n* **Test Steps:**\n  1. Attempt to log in with incorrect password 4 times consecutively.\n  2. Observe system behavior after each attempt.\n  3. Attempt to log in for the 5th time with the incorrect password.\n* **Expected Result:** \n  - Attempts 1-4 fail with standard incorrect password error.\n  - On the 5th failed attempt, the account locks, and an appropriate lock message is displayed (e.g., "Account locked due to multiple failed attempts. Try again in 15 minutes." ).\n* **Test Type:** Functional / Security / Business Rules\n* **Priority:** High\n* **Coverage Classification:** Business Rules / Error Handling / Negative Scenario\n\n---\n\n### **TC-LOG-010: Login Attempt on Locked Account within 15-Minute Window**\n* **Test Case ID:** TC-LOG-010\n* **Requirement Reference:** AC-10, Business Rules (Lock duration: 15 mins)\n* **Title:** Verify login is blocked even with correct credentials during the 15-minute lock period.\n* **Preconditions:** \n  - User account is currently locked due to 5 failed attempts (from TC-LOG-009).\n  - Current time is within the 15-minute lockout window.\n* **Test Data:** \n  - Email: `locked.user@example.com`\n  - Correct Password: `ValidPassword123`\n* **Test Steps:**\n  1. Enter the correct registered email and correct password.\n  2. Click the "Login" button.\n* **Expected Result:** \n  - Login is denied.\n  - Lockout message is shown indicating the account is temporarily locked (e.g., "Account is locked. Please try again later." ).\n  - User is not redirected to the Dashboard.\n* **Test Type:** Functional / Business Rules\n* **Priority:** High\n* **Coverage Classification:** Business Rules / Negative Scenario\n\n---\n\n### **TC-LOG-011: Account Unlocking After 15 Minutes (Simulated/Edge)**\n* **Test Case ID:** TC-LOG-011\n* **Requirement Reference:** AC-10, Business Rules (Lock duration: 15 mins)\n* **Title:** Verify user can log in successfully after the 15-minute lockout period expires.\n* **Preconditions:** \n  - Account was locked previously.\n  - 15 minutes have elapsed (simulated via mock clock or time expiration).\n* **Test Data:** \n  - Email: `loc